  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing WASH Technical Capacity Building Support For Sector in Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) team at OXFAM in Bangladesh has devised an Android -based application and web solution aimed at digitizing the database and implementing a prediction model for latrine scheduled desludging. This system enables IFSTN operators to efficiently schedule desludging teams in designated sanitation zones and forecast containment sludge volume for cost -effective desludging operations. The Android app incorporates features like spatial tracking, self -prediction models for desludging dates, colour -coded indicators for latrine status, complaint registration, and desludging reports. Meanwhile, the web app offers spatial maps, live infographics, and downloadable reports for enhanced monitoring capabilities. Recent field trials conducted in camps 3 and 4 have demonstrated substantial enhancements in desludging efficiency and resource utilization. However, proactive data recording during the initial phase is imperative for precise predictions, with accuracy progressively improving as more data is inputted into the system. Presently, the application is deployed in 14 camps under the office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR) Area of responsibility. With the allocated funds, we intend to: 1. Expand the application&apos;s usage to United Nations Children&apos;s Fund (UNICEF) and International Organisation for Migration (IOM) working areas, encompassing a total of 33 camps. This expansion will involve system upgrades to include latrine database for new camps, staff training, and preparation of unique latrine IDs. After successful hands -on training , system will be handed over to UNICEF and IOM for future Operation and Maintenance (O and M) (Server cost)  2. Upgrade the current model by addressing the following areas: &#x2022; Improving the prediction model: The current model, which analyses past data, achieved an accuracy rate of approximately 60% to 70% after year of testing. We aim to enhance this accuracy by comparing it with other solu</narrative>
  </description>
